<decompilertest>
<!--
    fastfailnoreturn: a Windows `int 0x29` (`__fastfail`) raises the stack pointer
    by eight bytes, which destroys the frame of every function that contains one.

    x86 SLEIGH lifts `INT imm8` to `intloc = swi(imm8); call [intloc]` (ia.sinc:3671)
    - a `call` with NO matching push, unlike every other x86 CALL, which lifts as
    `RSP = RSP - 8; push &next; call target`.  Nothing downstream knows that, so the
    interrupt is an ordinary modelled call and `x86-64-win.cspec`'s default
    `__fastcall` (extrapop="8" stackshift="8") hands eight bytes back after it.
    Stage model: S2 flow classification (`setup_callind_specs`).

    Layout (x86-64 Windows), the MSVC /GS + STL _STL_VERIFY shape reduced to one site:
      0x140001000  48 83 ec 28     sub  rsp,0x28
      0x140001004  48 89 4c 24 20  mov  [rsp+0x20],rcx   ; a local
      0x140001009  48 85 c9        test rcx,rcx
      0x14000100c  75 07           jne  0x140001015
      0x14000100e  b9 05 00 00 00  mov  ecx,5            ; FAST_FAIL_INCORRECT_STACK
      0x140001013  cd 29           int  0x29             ; __fastfail(5)
      0x140001015  48 8b 44 24 20  mov  rax,[rsp+0x20]
      0x14000101a  48 83 c4 28     add  rsp,0x28
      0x14000101e  c3              ret

    Were the interrupt to fall through, the join at 0x140001015 would be reached
    with two stack-pointer values eight bytes apart and the frame would stop being
    a constant offset from the spacebase: RSP itself becomes a `char *` local, and
    the load of the parameter's own slot degenerates into an offset off it.
    `__fastfail` never returns, so the block ends at the interrupt, the unbalanced
    stack pointer reaches no join, and the function is the one line it always was.

    Assert #1 pins the recovered body.  Asserts #2 and #3 pin the two artefacts of
    the unbalanced frame - RSP tracked as a variable, and the degenerate load off
    it - to zero occurrences.  Neither pins an SSA index.
-->
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:windows">
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x140001000" readonly="true">4883ec2848894c24204885c97507b905000000cd29488b4424204883c428c3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x140001000" name="fastfail_guard"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>lo fu fastfail_guard</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="FASTFAILNORETURN #1: the parameter is returned directly once the interrupt ends the flow" min="1" max="1">return a0;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FASTFAILNORETURN #2: the stack pointer never becomes a tracked variable" min="0" max="0">; // rsp</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FASTFAILNORETURN #3: the parameter's own stack slot never degenerates into an offset off a tracked stack pointer" min="0" max="0">\*\(unsigned long long \*\)&amp;v[0-9]+\[0x20\]</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
